    "result_text": "`AcceptanceTest` is the only runnable test class (the other two are support classes), and the full suite is green.\n\n## Summary\n\nAdded a `checkDigit` field to the Owner response equal to the Luhn check digit over the digits of `customerCode`:\n\n1. **`model/CustomerCode.java`** (new) \u2014 a helper with `checkDigit(String)` implementing the standard Luhn algorithm over the digits in the code, ignoring the formatting dashes. It mirrors the spec's algorithm (and the single source of truth for the mapper), matching the pattern of the existing `MembershipLevel` derivation helper.\n\n2. **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 added a read-only `checkDigit` integer property (0\u20139) to the `Owner` schema, so the generated `OwnerDto` carries the field.\n\n3. **`mapper/OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 mapped `checkDigit` via `CustomerCode.checkDigit(owner.getCustomerCode())`, consistent with the other derived-field expression mappings.\n\nThe new `AcceptanceTest.coreCheckDigitIsLuhnOfCustomerCode` passes and `BUILD SUCCESS` with no regressions.",
