    "final_verdict": "VERDICT: LGTM\n\nThe change matches the codebase's established idiom precisely, so there is nothing to improve structurally.\n\n- `OwnerMapper` already delegates every derived response field to a small single-purpose helper in the `model` package: `MembershipLevel.of`, `OwnerIdentity.of`, `ContactPreference.of`, `Regions.localityOf`. The new `CustomerCode.checkDigit(...)` slots into that exact pattern rather than inlining Luhn arithmetic into the mapper expression \u2014 logic is in the right unit.\n- The new class mirrors the convention of its siblings (`MembershipLevel`, `OwnerIdentity`): `final` class, private constructor, static derivation method, and javadoc naming it the single source of truth consumed by `OwnerMapper`. A maintainer would find it natural.\n- Taking a `String code` rather than the whole `Owner` is a reasonable (arguably cleaner) contract since the computation depends only on the code; the mapper passes `owner.getCustomerCode()`. No duplication, and the class is single-purpose, not a catch-all.\n- The OpenAPI addition is co-located with the sibling derived fields and documented consistently.\n\nNo changes needed.",
